\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {9}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {RQ2: breadth's stack gain depends on an identifier transform being present.} Breadth over the clean-code control, split by whether the stack contains an identifier transform, with the \emph  {difference} between the groups. The rule defining the split was fixed before the unseen-containing stimulus existed, which makes the second row an out-of-sample test of it. We report the difference because one interval excluding zero while another does not is not a test of the difference between them.}}{11}{table.caption.9}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:rq2_identifier}{{9}{11}{\textbf {RQ2: breadth's stack gain depends on an identifier transform being present.} Breadth over the clean-code control, split by whether the stack contains an identifier transform, with the \emph {difference} between the groups. The rule defining the split was fixed before the unseen-containing stimulus existed, which makes the second row an out-of-sample test of it. We report the difference because one interval excluding zero while another does not is not a test of the difference between them}{table.caption.9}{}}
